 "equipment_type": "Soft starter",
 "applies_to": "Eaton S811+ soft starters read through a C441 Ethernet module, per Table 99 of MN04200002E.",
 "summary": "The S811+ is Eaton's larger soft starter with full motor protection, metering and a configurable I/O block. Through the C441 Ethernet module it is reachable over Modbus TCP and RS-485 Modbus RTU. This map covers the adapter I/O registers, status, fault and warning words, single-word current, power and frequency monitors, the network control words (500/501) and the main protection and comm-loss settings.",
 "transport": [
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "Tables print register numbers starting at 1; the manual states that the Modbus register address is the register number minus 1 (field inputs, register 1, is address 0). The manual itself calls the control words 'Modbus reg #500' and '#501'."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "C441 Ethernet Module User Manual (C441R, C441T, C441U, C441V)",
  "doc_number": "MN04200002E",
  "revision_date": "2012-08",
  "url": "https://www.precision-elec.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/C441-Ethernet-Module-User-Manual-C441R-C441T-C441U-C441V.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 59-64 (section 7.5, Table 99)",
  "unofficial": true
 },
 "notes": [
  "Source is a distributor copy (precision-elec.com) of Eaton manual MN04200002E dated August 2012. Eaton lists a later edition (January 2016) at eaton.com, which could not be downloaded from this machine; check it for changes.",
  "Only registers that are clearly one 16-bit word are listed. Items printed with a gap after them (fault/fault lists 301, 318, 370; mains voltage 308; starts 311; RMS line and pole current blocks 328-357 apart from the averages; pole temperature 362) have no stated length or word order and are left out, as is the float FLA at 600.",
  "Torque, ramp, stop and start-delay settings without printed units (609-613, 615-622, 641, 681-683) and several trip thresholds without units in the table (652, 655, 657, 673, 674) are left out.",
  "Registers 503-507 are the S811+'s own Modbus port settings (baud default 19200, RTU default). With a C441U/C441V that port is the link to the adapter, so integrators reach this map over Modbus TCP; the adapter's serial settings are 159-163.",
  "Signedness is not stated in the manual; values are typed unsigned."
 ],
